    https://github.com/exelban/stats
    Copyright (c) 2019 Serhiy Mytrovtsiy
    MIT licence — https://github.com/exelban/stats/blob/master/LICENSE

    As of this writing Caliper contains no code from Stats. It is an
    independent implementation, and Stats is read as a reference — chiefly for
    the SMC and IOHID sensor keys that every Apple SoC generation renames,
    which their Modules/Sensors/values.swift has been accumulating since 2020,
    and for the failure modes their changelog has already paid for.

    Where that changes it is recorded here rather than left implicit. Any file
    carrying material from Stats keeps their copyright header above ours and
    says what was modified, and gains an entry under this heading naming the
    file and what was taken from it.

    This is not paperwork. The MIT licence grants everything it grants on one
    condition — that the notice travels with the copy — so keeping it is the
    price of the permission, not a courtesy on top of it. And a monitor that
    competes with Stats while standing on their work is the last project that
    should be quiet about doing so.
